The system combines three signals:
Signal 1 — Training load
|Load Z-score| < 1.5     NORMAL
1.5–2.0                  WATCH
≥ 2.0                    HIGH
Signal 2 — Readiness
Because low readiness is the concerning direction:
Readiness Z > -1.5       NORMAL
-2.0 to -1.5             WATCH
≤ -2.0                   LOW
Signal 3 — Load change
< 10%                    NORMAL
10–20%                   WATCH
≥ 20%                    HIGH
The three signals contribute to a decision score.
Decision Score
      ↓
0–1   GREEN
2–4   YELLOW
5+    RED
These are demonstration rules, not clinically validated athlete-risk thresholds.